{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Juan and Mary play a two-person game in which the winner gains 2 points and the loser loses 1 point. If Juan won exactly 3 games and Mary had a final score of 5 points, how many games did they play?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57cfc5b81b87ea5e8af046215b65c3ca04c33f73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 7 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"338\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If Juan won 3 games, then Mary lost 3 points. Mary must have had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108880936ebf093c88308f58baa4abe040466366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> points at the start, meaning she won 4 games. This makes a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfd07bedbde4872ca42d1804da88bb6339562616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 4 = \\boxed{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"23\" /> games.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Pro